{"name":"Bright Sage","hex":"#d1ceb4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sage (philosophy)","blocks":[{"text":"A sage, in classical philosophy, is someone who has attained wisdom. The term has also been used interchangeably with a 'good person', and a 'virtuous person'. Some of the earliest accounts of the sage begin with Empedocles' Sphairos. Horace describes the Sphairos as \"Completely within itself, well-rounded and spherical, so that nothing extraneous can adhere to it, because of its smooth and polished surface.\" Alternatively, the sage is one who lives \"according to an ideal which transcends the everyday.\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(philosophy)","wikidata":"Q2624172"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)","wikidata":"Q7399114"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"bright":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/En-us-bright.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/be/En-us-bright.ogg/En-us-bright.ogg.mp3"}],"sage":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/En-us-sage.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/79/En-us-sage.ogg/En-us-sage.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.6425},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.551875},{"title":"De Aus Dichtung und Sage (Hertz W) 180","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/De_Aus_Dichtung_und_Sage_%28Hertz_W%29_180.jpg/500px-De_Aus_Dichtung_und_Sage_%28Hertz_W%29_180.jpg","ratio":0.6931914893617022,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_Aus_Dichtung_und_Sage_(Hertz_W)_180.jpg","share":0.17375},{"title":"De Aus Dichtung und Sage (Hertz W) 209","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/De_Aus_Dichtung_und_Sage_%28Hertz_W%29_209.jpg/500px-De_Aus_Dichtung_und_Sage_%28Hertz_W%29_209.jpg","ratio":0.6931914893617022,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_Aus_Dichtung_und_Sage_(Hertz_W)_209.jp